---
import ServicePage from '../layouts/ServicePage.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---

<ServicePage
  title="Privacy Policy | Shore Leave"
  description="How Shore Leave collects, uses and protects your personal information under the New Zealand Privacy Act 2020."
  crumb="Privacy"
  h1="Privacy"
  lede="What we collect, why, and what you can do about it, under the New Zealand Privacy Act 2020."
  hideCta
>
  <article class="wrap pb-20 prose-sl max-w-[52rem]">
    <p>Last updated 1 November 2026.</p>
    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>{SITE.name} is run by {SITE.owners} in Auckland. Questions about privacy go to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> or {SITE.phoneDisplay}.</p>
    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>When you use the booking form, we collect your name, mobile, email, boat details, boat location, the services you want, your preferred dates, your restock list and notes, and how you heard about us.</p>
    <p>When you book, we may also hold access details for your boat, and before-and-after photos of the job.</p>
    <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To reply to you, quote the job and carry it out</li>
      <li>To keep records of the work we’ve done</li>
      <li>To contact you about your bookings</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We don’t sell your information, and we don’t send marketing without asking first.</p>
    <h2>Who sees it</h2>
    <p>We use a small number of service providers to run this site. They process information on our behalf, and some are based overseas, including in the United States.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Vercel</strong> hosts the website and provides cookieless visitor statistics.</li>
      <li><strong>Resend</strong> delivers the emails from the booking form.</li>
      <li><strong>Microsoft Clarity</strong> and <strong>Google Analytics</strong> show how the site is used. They only load if you say yes to the cookie banner.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>We keep booking records for as long as we need them for the job and for tax and legal records. If you never go ahead, we delete your enquiry when we no longer need it. Boat keys and access codes are returned or destroyed when you stop using the service.</p>
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>You can ask to see the personal information we hold about you and ask us to correct it. Contact us using the details above and we’ll respond as soon as we can. You don’t have to give us your information, but we can’t quote or do the job without it.</p>
    <p>If you’re not happy with how we’ve handled your information, you can complain to the <a href="https://www.privacy.org.nz/">Office of the Privacy Commissioner</a>.</p>
    <h2>Keeping it safe</h2>
    <p>We take reasonable steps to protect your information. If a privacy breach is likely to cause serious harm, we’ll tell you and the Privacy Commissioner, as the Act requires.</p>
  </article>
</ServicePage>
